{"kind":"report","text":"LS-7 route (a) refusal (4f8d35a1), and one upgrade-cohort room for U4 and LS-7.\n\n(1) The refusal. The prefix explains it, but the journal shows the name only indirectly.\n- Directory application item 8 (state created, the application of install item 2, Lending 0.4.0) holds publication [\"shelf/\"]. The read: `dap items directory` with type application, at Directory entry 18.\n- Lending declares that prefix (examples/lending/dap.application.json:15), and 0.5.0's semantic identifier equals 0.4.0's, so 0.5.0 asks for the same prefix.\n- Directory entry 18 is the creation tell from rules:16. It has 0 effects and 1 send, the refusing result. Rules 18 then records item 11 refused, install-route-refused.\n- `dap show` prints no message reason, so it does not show the result's refusal name. By elimination it is publication-prefix-in-use (base-directory.ts:96-102). The other creation guards are has-repository and application-capabilities, and both hold for a package with 0.4.0's repository and semantics.\n- No act releases the claim: \"a created one keeps it\" (base-directory.ts:11-13), and no act retires an application. So the shelf host cannot move to a second Lending item in this room.\n\n(2) Plan: one new room, cohort upgrade, on dap-lending.\n1. You: a new operator home and `dap install https://dap-lending.inguz.workers.dev --host artifacts --namespace \u003cnew namespace\u003e --cohort upgrade`. The cohort is per register (docs/cli.md:103), so this makes a new register. Then `dap create upgrade-witness`. `dap verify rules` in that home must name platform:rules@16.\n2. You install Counter 0.6.0 (581e5d26) and Lending 0.4.0 (1a5128d4). Both are trusted. Only Lending declares a prefix, so the two items do not conflict. Record both item numbers, the Directory, and each item's presentation (Counter 905a3f7e, Lending 188f7b84).\n3. You donate the stepladder in the new Library scope, before any upgrade.\n4. Me: one SCREEN_HOSTS head in apps/sandbox/wrangler.rollout.jsonc, with a full gate, then your sandbox deployment.\n   - lending-shelf.inguz.space moves to the new Directory and Lending item, presentation 188f7b84.\n   - A new row: counter-upgrade.inguz.space for the new Counter item, presentation 905a3f7e. counter.inguz.space stays on counter-witness item 20, so NF-7's witnessed host keeps its room.\n   - The sandbox route is *.inguz.space/*, so a new host needs no route change. Confirm the DNS name, as for lending-shelf on 16 Nov.\n   - Since U3 the matcher ignores the presentation, so neither row changes again after the upgrades.\n5. U4 continues: my marker head (gate running at 63841108) lands, you sign Counter 0.7.0, then my trust-row head, then your dap-lending deployment.\n6. Before the upgrades, with one member @upgrade-witness from one member invitation and a persistent profile:\n   - Counter: the screen at counter-upgrade.inguz.space joins and records one count. The footer has no release line in 0.6.0. The MCP cards read the same room.\n   - Lending: the 0.4.0 screen cannot verify a join (the GW-1 gap of LS-7 run 1). The before-read is therefore the journal (`dap items` on the Library: the stepladder available) plus a screenshot of the 0.4.0 screen's join form. No join is attempted.\n7. You: `dap application upgrade \u003ccounter item\u003e \u003curi\u003e --release \u003c0.7.0 id\u003e --request \u003ckey\u003e` and `dap application upgrade \u003clending item\u003e \u003curi\u003e --release sha256:1bda4e9b… --request \u003ckey\u003e`, both in place.\n8. After the upgrades, with the same profile:\n   - Counter: the footer shows \"Counter 0.7.0\" in [data-release]. The member key is the same, and the count and the journal carry across. The MCP cards are read again.\n   - Lending: the 0.5.0 screen at lending-shelf.inguz.space joins. Before the run I check whether the Lending page accepts `dap invite @upgrade-witness --device`. If it does, one member covers both screens. If not, a second member, which